---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | SuperCritical Materials"
  description="This Privacy Policy explains how SuperCritical Materials collects, uses and protects personal information when you visit supercritical.one."
>
  <PageHero title="Privacy Policy" />
  <article class="policy mx-auto grid w-[90%] gap-4 py-14 text-[15.8px] leading-[1.52] min-[981px]:px-[240px] min-[981px]:py-20">
    <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> November 2, 2026</p>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how SuperCritical Materials ("SuperCritical Materials," "we," "us") collects, uses and
      protects personal information when you visit supercritical.one (the "Site"), contact us, or subscribe to our
      newsletter.
    </p>
    <p>We do not sell products on this Site, and we do not sell or rent your personal information.</p>

    <h2 class="label mt-6 text-[24px] leading-snug text-accent">Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      SuperCritical Materials<br />
      Austin, TX USA<br />
      Email: <a href="mailto:tallen@supercritical.one">tallen@supercritical.one</a>
    </p>
    <p>We are the controller of the personal information described in this policy.</p>

    <h2 class="label mt-6 text-[24px] leading-snug text-accent">Information we collect</h2>
    <p><strong>Information you give us</strong></p>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
      <li><strong>Contact form:</strong> your name, email address, company, and anything you include in your message.</li>
      <li><strong>Newsletter signup:</strong> your email address (and name, if you provide it).</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Information collected automatically, only with your consent</strong></p>
    <p>
      If you accept analytics cookies, Google Analytics collects information about how you use the Site, such as pages
      viewed, time on page, approximate location (country/city), device and browser type, and how you arrived (for
      example, a search engine or LinkedIn). Google Analytics 4 does not log or store full IP addresses.
    </p>
    <p><strong>Information collected for security and site delivery</strong></p>
    <p>
      When you visit the Site, our hosting provider and the services below process basic technical data (such as your IP
      address and browser type) so the Site can load and be protected from spam and abuse.
    </p>

    <h2 class="label mt-6 text-[24px] leading-snug text-accent">How we use your information</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
      <li>To respond to your inquiries and communicate with you about our products and services.</li>
      <li>To send our newsletter, if you subscribed. Every email includes an unsubscribe link.</li>
      <li>To understand how the Site is used and improve it (only if you consent to analytics).</li>
      <li>To protect the Site and our forms from spam, fraud and abuse.</li>
      <li>To comply with legal obligations.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="label mt-6 text-[24px] leading-snug text-accent">Legal bases (EEA and UK visitors)</h2>
    <p>If you are in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, we rely on:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
      <li><strong>Consent</strong> for analytics cookies and our newsletter. You can withdraw consent at any time.</li>
      <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> to respond to your inquiries, operate and secure the Site, and prevent spam.</li>
      <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> where we must keep certain records.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="label mt-6 text-[24px] leading-snug text-accent">Cookies</h2>
    <p>We use a cookie banner so you can choose which non-essential cookies to allow.</p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Category</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
            <th>Examples</th>
            <th>When it's set</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Strictly necessary</td>
            <td>Remembers your cookie choices</td>
            <td><code>cc_cookie</code></td>
            <td>Always</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Analytics</td>
            <td>Measures Site usage via Google Analytics</td>
            <td><code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code></td>
            <td>Only if you accept</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      You can change your choices at any time using the <strong>Cookie settings</strong> link in the footer of every page.
      You can also block or delete cookies in your browser settings.
    </p>

    <h2 class="label mt-6 text-[24px] leading-snug text-accent">Service providers we use</h2>
    <p>We share personal information only with service providers that help us run the Site. Each processes data under its own privacy terms:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
      <li>
        <strong>Netlify</strong> (website hosting and contact form processing) –
        <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">netlify.com/privacy</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Analytics</strong> (Site analytics, only with your consent) –
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/privacy</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google reCAPTCHA</strong> (spam protection on our contact form) –
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/privacy</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Adobe Fonts</strong> (displays the typefaces used on the Site; your browser connects to Adobe's servers, which may receive your IP address) –
        <a href="https://www.adobe.com/privacy.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">adobe.com/privacy</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>[Newsletter provider, e.g. Mailchimp]</strong> (newsletter delivery) – [link to provider's privacy policy]
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may also disclose information if required by law or to protect our rights, or as part of a merger, acquisition or
      sale of assets.
    </p>

    <h2 class="label mt-6 text-[24px] leading-snug text-accent">International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Our service providers are based in, or process data in, the United States and other countries. Where personal
      information from the EEA or UK is transferred, we rely on appropriate safeguards such as the EU-U.S. Data Privacy
      Framework or Standard Contractual Clauses.
    </p>

    <h2 class="label mt-6 text-[24px] leading-snug text-accent">How long we keep information</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
      <li><strong>Contact form messages:</strong> as long as needed to respond and maintain our business relationship, then deleted.</li>
      <li><strong>Newsletter subscriptions:</strong> until you unsubscribe.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics data:</strong> 14 months, then automatically deleted.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="label mt-6 text-[24px] leading-snug text-accent">Your rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
      <li>access the personal information we hold about you;</li>
      <li>correct or delete it;</li>
      <li>object to or restrict how we use it;</li>
      <li>receive a copy in a portable format;</li>
      <li>withdraw consent at any time (this does not affect processing that already happened); and</li>
      <li>complain to your local data protection authority.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Residents of California and other U.S. states with privacy laws may have similar rights to know, correct and delete
      their information. We do not sell or "share" personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising.
    </p>
    <p>
      To make a request, email <a href="mailto:tallen@supercritical.one">tallen@supercritical.one</a>. We will respond
      within the time required by applicable law and will not discriminate against you for exercising your rights.
    </p>

    <h2 class="label mt-6 text-[24px] leading-snug text-accent">Children</h2>
    <p>The Site is intended for business audiences and is not directed to children under 16. We do not knowingly collect information from children.</p>

    <h2 class="label mt-6 text-[24px] leading-snug text-accent">Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect personal information, including encrypted (HTTPS)
      connections. No method of transmission over the internet is completely secure.
    </p>

    <h2 class="label mt-6 text-[24px] leading-snug text-accent">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The effective date at the top shows when it was last revised.</p>

    <h2 class="label mt-6 text-[24px] leading-snug text-accent">Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or your information:<br />
      SuperCritical Materials<br />
      Austin, TX USA<br />
      <a href="mailto:tallen@supercritical.one">tallen@supercritical.one</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .policy a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .policy table {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 36rem;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: #414042;
  }

  .policy th,
  .policy td {
    border: 1px solid #e6e6e6;
    padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem;
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  .policy th {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #333;
    background: #f5f5f7;
  }

  .policy code {
    color: #414042;
  }
</style>
